Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tegra_wm8962: do not dereference a missing runtime on card remove

tegra_wm8962_remove() looks up the PCM runtime of the card's only DAI link
and dereferences it unconditionally. When the codec is unbound first (for
example by writing the device name to the wm8962 driver's unbind file in
sysfs, or by a failed probe), the runtime has already been removed with the
codec component, snd_soc_get_pcm_runtime() returns NULL and the card's
remove hook oopses:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000570
  PC is at tegra_wm8962_remove+0x20/0x48
  tegra_wm8962_remove from snd_soc_card_remove+0x88/0x98
  ... from i2c_device_remove

Return early when there is no runtime or no codec DAI; there is no jack to
unregister in that case.

Observed on Microsoft Surface RT (Tegra 30, WM8962) on 7.0.1.

---
--- a/sound/soc/tegra/tegra_wm8962.c	2026-10-31 20:54:27.046164690 +0100
+++ b/sound/soc/tegra/tegra_wm8962.c	2026-10-31 20:54:27.061851719 +0100
@@ -101,10 +101,20 @@
 {
 	struct snd_soc_dai_link *link = &card->dai_link[0];
 	struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd = snd_soc_get_pcm_runtime(card, link);
-	struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_codec(rtd, 0);
-	struct snd_soc_component *component = codec_dai->component;
+	struct snd_soc_dai *codec_dai;
 
-	wm8962_mic_detect(component, NULL);
+	/*
+	 * The codec can be unbound before the card is removed (for example
+	 * through sysfs), and its PCM runtime is gone by then.
+	 */
+	if (!rtd)
+		return 0;
+
+	codec_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_codec(rtd, 0);
+	if (!codec_dai)
+		return 0;
+
+	wm8962_mic_detect(codec_dai->component, NULL);
 
 	return 0;
 }
